# Use EverOS for Memory

This project hosts a local [EverOS](https://github.com/EverMind-AI/EverOS) memory service. Prefer it for any durable memory (conversations, facts, preferences, agent skills), not ad-hoc files, SQLite side stores, or in-process dicts.

## How to persist

- Server: `./scripts/start-everos.sh` (default `http://127.0.0.1:8000`)
- Memory root: `./data/everos` (`EVEROS_ROOT`)
- Use **`/api/v2`** endpoints (not legacy `/api/v1` for new code):
  - `POST /api/v2/memory/add` — ingest messages
  - `POST /api/v2/memory/flush` — force extraction
  - `POST /api/v2/memory/search` — recall

## Conventions

- Scope with `app_id` / `project_id` (this repo: prefer `app_id=innerthink` unless a feature needs isolation).
- Store user identity in `sender_id` / `user_id` consistently across add and search.
- Do not invent a parallel memory DB or Markdown tree outside EverOS.
- Config and keys live in `.env` / `data/everos/everos.toml`; never commit secrets.

## When implementing agents or demos

Wire the agent loop to EverOS HTTP (add → flush at session end → search before answering) instead of stuffing long history into prompts alone.
